; The zone says its name servers are good for two seconds.  Its parent
; says an hour.  This is what a zone about to move does: it shortens its
; own NS TTL and waits, so that when the delegation changes everybody
; follows quickly.  It only works on a resolver which keeps the zone's
; number rather than the parent's.
$ORIGIN parentlong.
$TTL 3600
@	2	IN	SOA	ns.parentlong. root.parentlong. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@	2	IN	NS	ns.parentlong.
ns	3600	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
www	3600	IN	A	192.0.2.1
other	3600	IN	A	192.0.2.2
